.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dkim2\-exim
connects Exim to
.BR dkim2d (8)
in three separately configured operations:
.TP
.B inbound service
A long\-running
.B serve
process answers the source\-matched
.B local_scan
C module over a Unix socket and asks the daemon to verify each received
message.
This requires rebuilding the exact Exim source\-package revision with that
module; it is Linux\-only.
.TP
.B outbound signing
Exim runs
.B filter sign
as a
.B transport_filter
once per delivery: the complete message arrives on standard input, the signed
message leaves on standard output.
.TP
.B forwarding
.B filter revise
works the same way for mail this host forwards and adds a revision hop.
.PP
Each operation uses its own configuration file and capability.
Run every operation as the exact Exim user.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Run the inbound
.B local_scan
service until SIGTERM or SIGINT.
.TP
\fBfilter sign \-\-\fR \fIreturn\-path\fR \fIrecipients\fR
Sign one message for a local domain.
Pass Exim's
.B $dkim2_transport_filter_return_path
and
.B $pipe_addresses
as two separately quoted arguments after the literal
.BR \-\- .
.TP
\fBfilter revise \-\-\fR \fIlocal\-scan\-data\fR \fIreturn\-path\fR \fIrecipients\fR
Revise one forwarded message.
The first argument is Exim's
.B $local_scan_data
from the inbound service.
.PP
The filter commands take no options of their own and accept exactly the shown
arguments; anything else fails with exit status 75.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIstring\fR
absolute protected adapter configuration
.PP
The option must precede the command name.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The filter wrote the complete signed or revised message, or the service shut
down cleanly.
.TP
.B 75
Filter failure of any kind (EX_TEMPFAIL); Exim defers the delivery and retries.
Filters print nothing on standard output or standard error on failure.
.TP
.B 1
Service or command failure outside the filters, including a missing
.BR \-\-config .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/dkim2/exim.yaml
Inbound service configuration, as used in the Exim guide.
.TP
.IR /etc/dkim2/sign.yaml ", " /etc/dkim2/revise.yaml
Filter configurations for signing and forwarding.
.TP
.I /etc/default/dkim2\-exim
Service environment; sets
.B DKIM2_EXIM_UID
to the numeric UID of the Exim user.
.TP
.I /run/dkim2\-exim/
Runtime directory of the inbound socket (mode 0600, Exim UID only).
